 lid on his back this lid  seems to hold down someone who in time  will be born from among the undead  moving on because I don't think we're  prepared to understand that yet this  still shot appears to have leaked along  with all of the new info maybe it's a  scene from an upcoming trailer or  something what we see are ironclad  knights standing around in graves  whether they're looking inside the  graves or rising from the graves is  unclear  regardless look at the sword that  they're wielding it's undoubtedly a  replica of artorias sword and in fact  these swords are viewable in another  screenshot behind hawkwood at filing  shrine Artorius was a legendary night of  Gwyn and apparently he had great  influence because his weapon has been  passed down throughout the ages it  appears in Dark Souls 2 for example in  Dark Souls 3 though it looks like  someone has started smithing replicas of  it and speaking of Gwyn we learn about  one of his successors here as well this  translates to small man who calls  himself the king of kindling it's worth  noting that Lord of cinder is actually  king of kindling in Japanese he calls  himself Courtland laureth and he sits on  one of the five thrones at Firelink  shrine proclaiming himself to be the  lord of cinder interesting to note that  there are five Thrones perhaps there's  been one for every Lord of cinder in the  past this king is the self-proclaimed  lord of cinder perhaps he doesn't truly  live up to that title in some way and  finally he calls himself lute Leth the  war we explore in the network test used  to actually be called the wall of Lord  left and even though it's now called the  wall of lothric it's likely the domain  of this  tiny King additionally a player hoists a  small ringed banner upon the high wall  of lothric the birthplace of the former  king of kindling and company is spread  out below as though in a heap there are  a lot of landmarks in this screenshot so  if you're interested to learn about all  the different areas we've seen so far  and how they correlate with one another  then I've linked a really cool post by  TEDx in the description this next  screenshot shows a Pyromancer fighting  misshapen maggot like things there is a  reference here about how he's using  primitive magic the same sort of word  that was used for pyromancers in Dark  Souls 1 these are the sages who studied  at the great archive these swordsmen are  candlesticks that light the guiding  fires and they're covered in wax so that  they are not imprisoned by the cursed  magic of the books all this talk of  curses and archives it makes me think of  seats 2 main from Dark Souls 1 and there  are references to more dragons this is  an old ruin on a peak above the clouds  those that walk the path of the dragon  are directed to this place but the path  that leads here has been long lost in a  world that has been endlessly struggling  with light and dark this path of grey  dragons might be a pretty valid path in  Dark Souls 3 and finally a screenshot of  a dirty beast that looks kind of like  Amelia crossed with the cleric beast so  from all of this from all of the  screenshots that we've seen we realized  that a lot of the tropes and settings  from previous games they're still going  to be in Dark Souls 3 we have fire  keepers we have a filing shrine and one  of the translations even mentions that  we are on our way to becoming the lord  of cinder which in essence probably  means linking the flame the world is  like a pendulum swinging between light  and  and the thing at the center is linking  the flame when the flame is linked it's  like that pendulum gets pushed in one  direction or another yet it always  returns to the center nothing ever  really changes in Dark Souls 3 though it  seems like this time we're approaching  things from the side of the un-- kindled  instead of the undead it feels like  everything has been flipped  instead of humanity there are embers  instead of playing as an undead 