 this is  blood-borne  all in all it's a cool little gameplay  sequence because you have to fight while  thinking constantly about that threat  from above the difference is in Demon  Souls where this sort of situation  played out at least you could see what's  firing at you this ambush is pretty  nicely timed it plays upon your desire  to find shelter and punishes you for  sort of getting the hell out of there  the lighting and the darkness in this  room looks pretty nice  this next scene has us walk through this  sacred place and I call it a sacred  place because there are petals rising up  towards the sky which definitely kind of  helps with that sacred feel hollows pray  to a giant tree which is in keeping with  the theme that we've seen in the demo  where gray hollows prayed to trees and  where some of those trees even had  hollows growing into them and it turns  out this tree isn't too different  perhaps this is what one of those  hollows successfully grew into generally  I don't like bosses that have you  balancing the actual boss with a lot of  little mobs usually that feels a little  bit cheap like a cheap way to increase  the difficulty thankfully though this  boss like the spears earlier appears to  target the mobs as well as yourself also  notice the weapon that were willing  it's the murakumo one of my favorite  weapons in the series actually we get to  see its webinar in action it seems to be  this long flowing spinning attack  the fight ends with the floor collapsing  as this boss enters his second phase a  lot of blood-borne bosses also made use  of this boss phase mechanic and I think  that we're seeing most bosses in Dark  Souls 3 make use of it as well and  that's it guys  big shout out to law master Naja who  helped with the translation as well as  Alex Roe who provided these really  beautiful Dark Souls themed music tracks  from his new album darksign you really  should check it out listening to this  soundtrack is like listening to what an  upcoming Seoul's Games soundtrack is  going to be there's so so many beautiful  tracks on there and thanks for watching  guys we'll see you in February

